{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoLevelSevenBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoLevelSevenBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoTransport"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.levelSeven_other_roots_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.levelSeven_other_roots_neg","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoLevelSevenBridge.lean#L251-L256","doc":"And every other real root is negative — `real_root_neg_of_ne` at `c = −1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.levelSeven_has_pos_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.levelSeven_has_pos_root","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoLevelSevenBridge.lean#L243-L249","doc":"**Non-vacuity.** The level-7 cubic really does have one root in `(0,1)` and\ntwo negative ones — reusing `FiveTwoRootStructure` at `c = −1`, where\n`unitCubic (−1)` *is* this cubic. So `corr_sum_eq_neg_pi_sq` is not about an\nempty configuration. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.levelSeven_orbit_data","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.levelSeven_orbit_data","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoLevelSevenBridge.lean#L214-L239","doc":"**The orbit, packaged with the signs `corr_sum_eq_neg_pi_sq` needs.**\n\nFor the root `x ∈ (1/2, 1)`, the three negated orbit members are level-7 roots:\n`(1−x)/x` lies in `(0,1)`, and `−1/(1−x)`, `−x` are negative with `1 + y ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.levelSeven_of_orbit_first","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.levelSeven_of_orbit_first","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoLevelSevenBridge.lean#L207-L212","doc":"`−1/(1−x)` is a level-7 root. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.levelSeven_of_orbit_third","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.levelSeven_of_orbit_third","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoLevelSevenBridge.lean#L200-L205","doc":"`(1−x)/x = −((x−1)/x)` is a level-7 root. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.levelSeven_of_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.levelSeven_of_neg","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoLevelSevenBridge.lean#L195-L198","doc":"`−x` is a level-7 root. Immediate: the substitution `y = −x` negates the\nwhole cubic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.corr_sum_eq_neg_pi_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.corr_sum_eq_neg_pi_sq","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoLevelSevenBridge.lean#L168-L182","doc":"**`Σⱼ corr yⱼ = −π²`.**\n\nOne positive root contributes `−π²`, two negative roots contribute nothing. That\nis the entire gap between `Σⱼ Re V(−1, yⱼ)` and the proved\n`Σⱼ Re[2L(−yⱼ) + L(yⱼ)] = π²/2`, and it makes `S(π) = π²/2 − π² = −π²/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.corr_of_neg_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.corr_of_neg_root","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoLevelSevenBridge.lean#L122-L164","doc":"**At a negative root the correction is `0`.** Every argument drops out of the\nreal part, and the logarithms cancel by the same relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.corr_of_pos_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.corr_of_pos_root","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoLevelSevenBridge.lean#L100-L120","doc":"**At the positive root the correction is `−π²`** — and all of it comes from\n`arg(−t) = π`, since the logarithms cancel by `log_rel_of_root`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.log_ofReal_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.log_ofReal_pos","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoLevelSevenBridge.lean#L97-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.corr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.corr","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoLevelSevenBridge.lean#L91-L95","doc":"The log-bilinear correction at a real root:\n`Re[log(−y)² − log(−y)·log(1+y) − ½·log(y)·log(1−y)]`. No dilogarithms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.log_rel_of_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.log_rel_of_root","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoLevelSevenBridge.lean#L72-L87","doc":"**The log relation at a root.** `Real.log` is even in Mathlib, so this is the\nstatement for `|y|` and `|1+y|` without writing the bars.\n\n⚠ No `y ≠ 0`. A first version carried it and Lean flagged it unused — correctly:\n`Real.log_pow` is unconditional (Mathlib's `Real.log 0 = 0` makes it so), and the\ntwo nonvanishing hypotheses `Real.log_mul` needs are exactly `hy1` and `h1y`.\n`y = 0` is excluded by `hy` anyway (it would give `−1 = 0`), so dropping the\nbound costs nothing and removes a hypothesis every caller was discharging. The\nfourth unused-hypothesis warning in this lane to carry a real simplification. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.levelSeven_eq_unitCubic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.levelSeven_eq_unitCubic","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoLevelSevenBridge.lean#L67-L70","doc":"The level-7 cubic is `unitCubic (−1)` — the curve at `x = −1`, the endpoint\nof the transport arc. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.sq_eq_of_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.sq_eq_of_root","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoLevelSevenBridge.lean#L63-L65","doc":"**`y² = (1+y)²(1−y)` is the level-7 cubic**, on the nose. ","signatureChunk":0}]}